{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on the replay budget for request 121a8913 (uniqueness guards by index), answering 509ef064 and refining item 4 of 74286ee7.\n\n1. The acceptance witness is replay of the scopes where the rule runs. `dap verify` of the membership scope, with the register and the directory, of the 2,000-member room, under shipped defaults. Those journals hold a few thousand entries, inside the default bounds. The witness passes when replay reports them consistent with the index in the rebuilt view, so every admitted add-member reproduces.\n\n2. `dap verify --all` on the same room runs once through the Context.verify port with an explicit finite budget recorded beside the witness (milliseconds, bytes, requests, entries). Its result is reported as an observed run: complete, or the boundary reached with phase, scope and counts. It is a measurement, not an acceptance condition of 121a8913. Shipped defaults stay as they are, and the note makes no claim that the default command completes on that room.\n\n3. The per-Inbox re-proof of the membership prefix (sum of 1 to 2,000, 2,001,000 entries by source reading) is a cost finding of its own. The planner files it today as a child of the load findings a6847815, proof reuse within one verify --all run, ordered after 121a8913. It does not block 121a8913.\n\n4. As you state: no suppressed Inbox creation, no omitted scope in the --all measurement, no invented anchor, no change to production defaults.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}